Beyond, whenever the target uses a Supernatural Power, the illusion of a Cruac Viod Creature is created in the mind of the target. The Illusion, taking the form of darkness we with animal parts attacks the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:51:41-07:00","id":990282,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think abyssal creatures should not Count as kin: the opposite/perversion of everything that is (like the lie) or should be (the supernal realms), they are not of the dark mother. They are anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T05:45:53-07:00","id":990376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/859866-weird-kinships?p=990282#post990282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think abyssal creatures should not Count as kin: the opposite/perversion of everything that is (like the lie) or should be (the supernal realms), they are not of the dark mother. They are anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that while a lot of Abyssal creatures wouldn't be considered Family some would.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T06:42:20-07:00","id":990384,"title":"","content":"Anything &quot;Perverted&quot; by the Void would probably ping as Kin... anything of the Void Wholesale wouldn't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T07:06:37-07:00","id":990393,"title":"","content":"I have this crazy opinion that the Abyss is more reliant on human failings and fears than Mages would like to admit it does. So a lot of it is valid for Kinship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T09:33:56-07:00","id":990458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/859866-weird-kinships?p=990393#post990393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this crazy opinion that the Abyss is more reliant on human failings and fears than Mages would like to admit it does. So a lot of it is valid for Kinship.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I have to admit that in my headcanon,i consider the mage World view (supernal truths, The fallen World is a shadow and a lie, And The Abyss Is an unreality Made Through That fall using anything it can to invade and destroy Everything else) to be the &quot;rightest&quot;. So I'd agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3981_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3981\" data-vbnamecard=\"3981\">RickmanUK</a>. But with your justification, you could make it work easily like that, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T15:01:28-08:00","id":1016760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/859866-weird-kinships?p=990384#post990384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything &amp;quot;Perverted&amp;quot; by the Void would probably ping as Kin... anything of the Void Wholesale wouldn't be.</div> </div> </div> </div> Makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T18:46:16-08:00","id":1016860,"title":"","content":"What about Kinship with Idigam? Each one is unique, but they are all extremely mercurial and adaptable creatures who can twist others into monstrous servants or tools. A Nightmare based on them would probably focus on mimicking their Essence Shaping powers. I'd call this Nightmare &quot;Your Shape Is Not Your Own&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:30:26-08:00","id":1017028,"title":"","content":"OK, here is my attempt at writing the Nightmare mentioned in the previous post. It's quite powerful, but pursuing Kinship with Idigam is no easy task. Also, the entities altered by this Nightmare are under no compulsion to obey the Beast, but he may subtly direct their behavior by choosing the right traits. <br /> <br /> <b>Your Shape Is Not Your Own</b> [Idigam Kinship]<br /> <br /> <b>Dicepool</b>: Manipulation + Satiety vs Resistance + Rank<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast gains the ability to perceive and interact with ghosts and spirits in Twilight. If he can already do this through another power, add +1 to his dice pool. When targeting these entities, he may imitate the Ghost Manipulation or Spirit Manipulation powers of the Idigam, replacing Rank with Lair.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Beast can impose the nature of his Horror on a spirit or ghost, rather than only shifting around their pre-existing traits. The ghost or spirit gains a number of Numina, Influence dots and/or Dread Power dots equal to the Beast\u2019s Lair. These must reflect powers the Beast possesses.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast can force a ghost or spirit to merge with a living being for a scene. The resulting hybrid is a pseudo-Claimed with the ephemeral\u2019s Essence pool and all of its Influences, Numina and Dread Powers. For its other traits, use the Brief Nightmare rules with the ephemeral\u2019s Rank as a guideline.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The changes caused by this Nightmare last for a number of days equal to Lair rather than a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}